Title    Combined sprinkler and hydrant network - worked example
Project  PROJECT Hardy Cross solver demonstration model
Project  JOB HC-DEMO-002
Project  DESIGNER A Designer
Project  REVISION A
Project  DATE 2026-09-10
Project  STANDARD AS 2118.1
Project  DATA_SOURCE Hycadia pipe and fitting database - pipe dimensions and fitting equivalent lengths
Units    FLOW=LPM PRESSURE=KPA LENGTH=M DIAMETER=MM
Method   HW
Option   TOL_FLOW 0.01
Option   TOL_LOOP 0.005
Option   MAXITER 3000

Node     T1 0.0
Node     J1 0.0
Node     J2 0.0
Node     TM 0.0
Node     K1 0.0
Node     A 10.0
Node     B 10.0
Node     C 10.0
Node     D 10.0
Node     HY 10.0
Node     X 10.0
Node     X2 10.0
Node     Y 10.0
Node     Y2 10.0

Use      BORE
Pipe     M1 J2 A 30.0 150.0 C=120 EQV=8.0
Pipe     M2 K1 B 60.0 150.0 C=120 EQV=12.0
Pipe     G1 A B 40.0 100.0 C=120
Pipe     G2 B C 40.0 100.0 C=120
Pipe     G3 C D 40.0 100.0 C=120
Pipe     G4 D A 40.0 100.0 C=120
Pipe     G5 A C 55.0 80.0 C=120
Pipe     BR1 D X 10.0 50.0 C=120
Pipe     BR2 C Y 12.0 50.0 C=120
Pipe     BR3 C HY 15.0 100.0 C=120

Pump     PMP1 T1 J1 0 850 2500 800 4000 600

Supply   SUP1 T1 STATIC 200
Supply   SUP2 TM CURVE 0 1000 3000 700 6000 300

BFP      BFP1 J1 J2 0 0 1000 25 2000 55 3000 95
PRV      PRV1 TM K1 DP=150
Orifice  OP1 X X2 DP=80 DN=50
Orifice  OP2 Y Y2 BORE=22 DN=50

Head     S1 X2 K=80 P=50
Head     S2 Y2 K=115 Q=225
Hydrant  HYD1 HY Q=1200 P=250
HoseReel HR1 A K=7.5 P=220
Flow     FF1 B Q=300 MINP=200
